This is a snapshot of the export through 4 October 2026, not a live queue. Report IDs are
deduplicated before the causes are counted. The tenant's locale and booking form establish the
cause; intake tags are only guesses.

## Cause breakdown

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The parser row is the shared parser defect: it reads dates month first for day-first tenants.
The booking-v3 hint row is a separate form defect: its `MM/DD/YYYY` instruction conflicts with
the day-first order used to interpret submissions. File one ticket for each cause; fixing one
path does not correct the other.

## Reports over time

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

Five reports listed in the desk notes describe a one-day move and remain in the parser group;
they are not an additional cause.

